    {'key':'young','question':'How do I choose a play centre for a young child?','answer':'Look for an easy-to-navigate space with an area for younger children and adult accompaniment. Ask whether it is separated from older children’s active games. Amburan Kids has Sweet City and Moka Kids offers play areas; confirm the particular age requirements and rules before visiting.'},
    {'key':'school','question':'Where could we go with a school-age child?','answer':'Consider Kinderland for role-play, Bricobilandia for construction sets and Hello Park for interactive games. These are different formats: follow your child’s interest and check the requirements for the chosen activity.'},
    {'key':'tickets','question':'How much does a visit to a Baku play centre cost?','answer':'Compare the total cost: child, accompanying adult, time and separate games. Prices may vary by day, area and branch. Check the listing and confirm the tariff with the centre; a missing price does not mean free admission.'},
    {'key':'supervision','question':'Can I leave my child and go elsewhere?','answer':'Staff presence does not automatically mean a childcare service. Confirm whether visits without a parent are allowed, the minimum age, who accepts responsibility and how they contact you. Unless arrangements are confirmed, plan to stay nearby.'},
    {'key':'birthday','question':'Can we hold a birthday party at a play centre?','answer':'Ask the chosen branch about its package: numbers of children and adults, duration, room, host, food, cake and cancellation terms. Ordinary admission does not mean a party or private room is included.'},
    {'key':'rain','question':'Where can children play on a rainy day?','answer':'Indoor play centres in shopping complexes can be an option. Check that the play area itself is open: its hours may differ from the shops or shopping centre.'},
    {'key':'quiet','question':'How can I choose if noise and bright lights bother my child?','answer':'Ask about music, projections, crowd levels and somewhere to take a break. Do not assume weekdays are always quiet. Choose a familiar type of play for a first visit and leave room to finish early.'},
